From 62c67ad73742e6cbab9af19b7afdef82fc3f003c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:01:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure connection limits and relative
 data-directory startup

Snapshot signed connection and descriptor limits without changing startup
selection. Keep the relative datadir argument separate from the working
directory instead of labelling it an absolute file.path. Preserve Info
severity and readable diagnostics, including rate-limit disabling.

A real-node fixture checks the selected limit, logger setting, and restart
with a relative datadir against numeric/raw JSON and exact old text.
Platform resource reduction and Avalanche increase branches retain exact
reviewed expressions; they are not newly forced by this fixture.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py==0.51.0; from the commit's parent):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/connection-startup-diagnostics.json --apply

git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/init.cpp

Handwritten: focused functional assertions. Registry append is an explicit
reviewed support adjustment in the scripted catalog, without renumbering.

Coordinator ordered integration (2026-10-20):
Existing causal fixes and mechanical namespace/format adaptations are folded at their first responsible owner. Exact inputs and prefix adaptations are recorded in integration-next final delivery; original author provenance is retained.
